    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d143-a1">

                <pb facs="0319" n="219" sameAs="frus:frus1884/pg219"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure in No. 784.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. McCormack to the
                            President.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >People Office, Tipperary</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1883-11-28"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >November</hi> 28, 1883</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I beg to inform you that I am a citizen of
                    the United States; I have been incarcerated in a British bastile for nearly five
                    months by the British Government, without knowing for what. My case I shall
                    prove in due course, but in the interval I shall ask you to take the same care
                    of me as has the British Government in the case of the Rev. Mr. Shaw.</p>
                <p>In my case you will be good enough to ask of the British Government £10,000, and
                    shall it not be forthcoming in due course, I will have to appeal to my fellow
                    citizens of the United States.</p>
                <p>I send a copy of this to Mr. Lowell, and to many of my fellow-citizens at your
                    side of the Atlantic.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>JOHN R. McCORMACK.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
